Actually, summoning hordes of mostly-harmless monsters is a
considerable advantage to high-powered players: you can use them as a
buffer between you and truly threatening monsters when you need time to
recover. Therefore you might want to throw in the odd soldier/sarge
from time to time. It also makes more sense to me to have the law
summoned every time you remove the handcuffs (parole tagging system?)
rather than on #invoke. It would certainly make changing armour more of
a pain. Although you lose #invoke's timeout, your use of this feature
will still be limited by access to sources of unlocking/ remove curse,
and if you have the cuffs nerf spellcasting, you could restrict that to
scrolls and wands.

Would the handcuffs take up the gloves slot BTW? You'd have to make
sure they didn't offer 'trice-proofing if they do.

Just had a nice idea for the quest: Your quest leader's home level is a
no-teleport prison that you have to break into. This is the prison you
escaped from before beginning the game. You find your leader, an
ex-cellmate, in a doorless iron-bar cell. The quest leader is The
Prisoner of Zenda. He actually has the quest artifact with him, but you
can't get into the cell to retrieve it. However, you just happen to be
his/ her double (as per the film/ book), so you can impersonate him in
order to gain access to the other quest levels and fulfil your mission,
which is to kill the nemesis who holds the only item that can unlock
your quest leader's cell - the bell of opening (charge must be
guaranteed at least 0:2). You free Zenda, and in gratitude he gives you
his only possession, which is the magic handcuffs.

Another interesting quest leader could be the man in the iron mask,
with the mask as the quest artifact (obtained in a similar style to the
mission outlined above.)

Also, assuming you're still wearing it, your quest leader should be
able to remove your ball and chain on request. Or at least put a
guaranteed wand of opening / ?oRC somewhere on the home level. You have
to give these guys a break somewhere you know.



